The '''Karthon Chop Fields''' was a scrap yard used as a correction facility by the [[New Republic]]. Materials from the yard were used to construct the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]], prior to its [[Battle of Endor|destruction]] in [[4 ABY]]. In [[9 ABY]], the ex-[[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Sniper|sharpshooter]] [[Migs Mayfeld]] was sentenced to the Chop Fields for fifty [[Standard year|years]]. Wanting Mayfeld's help, the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] used the help of the New Republic [[Marshal]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]] to free the ex-Imperial, taking Mayfeld offworld aboard the [[Firespray-31-class patrol and attack craft|''Firespray-31''-class patrol and attack craft]] ''[[Slave I]]''. The criminal [[Scurto Tobbs]] was serving a 45-year sentence for transport of class 4 contraband in the Karthon Chop Fields at the same time as Mayfeld.

==Description==
The Karthon Chop Fields was a correction facility and scrapyard on [[Karthon]] where the [[New Republic]] sent [[prisoner]]s to serve time,<ref name="Chapter 14">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 14: The Tragedy}}</ref> using prison labor to scrap old [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[starship]]s and other equipment, including the cockpits of [[TIE series|TIE fighters]]. A model of [[mobile loading gantry]] was used to help move the materiel. Prisoners there were given uniforms and tools, toiling in the scrap heaps with [[N5 sentry droid]]s overseeing them.<ref name="Chapter 15">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 15: The Believer}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|What do you want with him?''"<br />"''I need to spring him to help me locate Moff Gideon's light cruiser.|Cara Dune and Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 14" />}}
Materials from the Karthon Chop Fields were used for construction on the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]],<ref name="Mando Handbook" /> which was [[Battle of Endor|destroyed]] in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="4 ABY" /> After the fall of the Empire, the New Republic used the scrap fields for prison labor.<ref name="Chapter 15" /> In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">{{MandoDate|6}}</ref> [[Migs Mayfeld]],<ref name="Chapter 14" /> an ex-Imperial [[Sniper|sharpshooter]] who had been apprehended during the [[Bothan-Five incident|breakout]] aboard the [[New Republic]] [[New Republic Correctional Transport|prison ship]]<ref name="Chapter 6">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 6: The Prisoner}}</ref> ''[[Bothan-5]]''<ref name="Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref> near the [[Dilestri system]], was sent to serve fifty [[Standard year|years]] in the Karthon Chop Fields for his involvement in the mission and the [[death]] of an [[Lant Davan|officer]] about the [[starship]]. Around the same time as Mayfeld's imprisonment, another [[human]] [[gender|male]], [[Scurto Tobbs]], was serving a 45-year sentence for transport of class 4 contraband at the Chop Fields.<ref name="Chapter 14" /> 

[[File:Migs_on_Karthon.png|thumb|left|300px|Migs Mayfeld is approached by N5 sentry droid at the Karthon Chop Fields]]
[[Din Djarin]], a [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] who had led Mayfeld into the hands of the New Republic,<ref name="Chapter 6" /> sought to free Mayfeld in order to help him locate an Imperial [[Gideon's light cruiser|light cruiser]] belonging to [[Moff]] [[Gideon]].<ref name="Chapter 14" /> He traveled to Karthon Chop Fields with the New Republic [[Marshal]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]], the bounty hunter [[Boba Fett]] and the [[assassin]] [[Fennec Shand]]. Using her powers under the New Republic, Dune had an [[Unidentified N5 sentry droid|N5 sentry droid]] lead her to Mayfeld, and she freed him from his shackles. Dune then led him back to Fett's [[Firespray-31-class patrol and attack craft|''Firespray-31''-class patrol and attack craft]],<ref name="Chapter 15" /> ''[[Slave I]]'',<ref name="Slave I DB">{{Databank|boba-fetts-starship|''Slave I''}}</ref> and the ex-Imperial left with Djarin's group. After the completion of their [[Mission to Morak|mission]], Mayfeld prepared to return to his imprisonment in the Chop Fields, but Dune allowed him to walk away free instead.<ref name="Chapter 15" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|In episode, the miniature model maker built 12, 15 TIE fighter balls and this wonderful table top set to be visualized on the screen. That's an example of taking the practical models and bringing it into today's technology.|Visual effects supervisor [[Richard Bluff]]|<ref name="Disney Gallery">{{DisneyGallery|Disney Gallery: The Mandalorian: Making of Season Two|Making of Season Two}}</ref>}}
[[File:Karthon-concept-art.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of the Karthon Chop Fields by Erik Tiemens]]
The Karthon Chop Fields was first mentioned in "[[Chapter 14: The Tragedy]]" of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which was directed by [[Robert Rodriguez]]<ref name="Chapter 14" /> and aired on [[December 4]] [[2020]].<ref name="D23">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-december-2020|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in December 2020}}</ref> The location then first appeared in the following episode "[[Chapter 15: The Believer]]," which was directed by [[Rick Famuyiwa]]<ref name="Chapter 15" /> and released on [[December 11]] 2020.<ref name="D23" /> The set was designed as a miniature model, which included 12 to 15 TIE fighter balls, and then scanned and projected in The Volume, a production space with wrap-around LED screens to show CGI backgrounds.<ref name="Disney Gallery" />

